.Ss Conflict resolutions
.Bl -bullet -compact
.It
\fB#163 (Justfile):\fP
.Ql "main"
had already disabled the
.Ql "run" Ns No "/" Ns Ql "debug" Ns No "/"
.Ql "tty" Ns No "/" Ns Ql "daemon" Ns No "/" Ns Ql "client" Ns No "/" Ns Ql "client-tty" Ns No "/" Ns Ql "quick" Ns No "/" Ns Ql "compile" Ns No "/…"
recipes (replaced commands with echo notices), so #163's quoting of those bodies was moot.
Kept the disabled bodies; the quoting auto-applied to the still-active recipes
.No \&( Ns Ql "default" ,
.Ql "run-built" ,
.Ql "clean" ,
.Ql "clean-all" ).
.It
\fB#145 (module wrappers):\fP
.Ql "main"
had renamed
.Ql "cfg.package"
→
.Ql "selectedPackage"
in
.Ql "module-system.nix"
since the PR was opened.
Re-applied #145's
.Ql "--"
additions onto the current
.Ql "selectedPackage"
wrapper bodies, keeping #159's
.Ql "eca"
entries.
.Ql "module.nix"
auto-merged.
.It
\fB#155 (CI restructure):\fP supersedes #158 and #162.
The auto-merge produced a Frankenstein
.Ql "ci.yml"
(#155's PR-only trigger + #158's push-gated cachix steps that can never fire).
Rewrote
.Ql "ci.yml"
to the clean intent: lean PR-only workflow with \fBpull-only\fP cachix on PRs (no
.Ql "CACHIX_AUTH_TOKEN"
— honours #158's \(dqno writer token on PR events\(dq).
.Ql "pages.yml"
was a modify/delete conflict (us=#162, them=#155 delete) → resolved as delete; the new
.Ql "deploy.yml"
carries #162's intent (per-job
.Ql "pages" Ns No "/" Ns Ql "id-token"
perms,
.Ql "build-docs" Ns No "/" Ns Ql "deploy"
gated
.Ql "if: refs/heads/main" )
and handles push-time cache pushes with the token.
.El
.Ss Note — #160 is a real fix, not cosmetic
.Ql "flake.lock"
has two nixpkgs nodes:
.Ql "nixpkgs"
(rev
.Ql "4df1b885" ,
a \fItransitive\fP dep of the
.Ql "jylhis-emacs"
input) and
.Ql "nixpkgs_2"
(rev
.Ql "ffa10e26" ,
the \fBroot\fP flake's actual nixpkgs).
The standalone
.Ql "emacs.nix" Ns No "/" Ns Ql "emacs-jylhis.nix"
were reading the wrong node
.No \&( Ns Ql "lock.nodes.nixpkgs" ).
#160 switches to
.Ql "lock.nodes.root.inputs.nixpkgs"
→
.Ql "nixpkgs_2"
→
.Ql "ffa10e26" ,
realigning the standalone build with the flake and restoring the cache-parity invariant.
Verified post-merge that
.Ql "emacs.nix"
now resolves nixpkgs to
.Ql "ffa10e26" .
(The verification snippet in
.Ql "CLAUDE.md"
still references the old
.Ql "lock.nodes.nixpkgs.locked" ;
updating it is an optional follow-up — #160 only patched the copy inside
.Ql "emacs.nix" .)
