.Ql "jylhis-emacs"
rebuilt from source (expected — #165 bumped its rev; not yet cached).
.It
.Ql "nix build --builders '' .#emacs"
→
.Ql "emacs-git-20260604.0" ,
.Ql "GNU Emacs 32.0.50" .
.It
.Ql "devenv test"
→ exit 0 (all dev-environment
.Ql "enterTest"
assertions).
.It
.Ql "just verify"
→ OK on
.Ql "nixpkgs" ,
.Ql "treefmt-nix" ,
.Ql "emacs-overlay" .
.El
.Ss Notes
.Bl -bullet -compact
.It
The pre-existing
.Ql "statix.toml"
uses
.Ql "[disabled]"
as a table; the installed
.Ql "statix"
rejects it
.No \&( Ns Ql "TOML parse error … invalid type: map, expected a sequence" )
but falls back to defaults and \fBexits 0\fP, so the
.Ql "statix"
check still passes.
Not caused by these merges; fixing the config format
.No \&( Ns Ql "disabled = [\(dqrepeated_keys\(dq]" )
